- **router6 can ping pc15 (172.18.51.15)** at 0% loss ✓
- **router6 can ping pc11 (192.168.200.11)** at 0% loss ✓
- But the nftables FORWARD chain on router6 reveals **DROP rules on `iifname "eth2"`** (counters: 55 ICMP, 27 UDP packets actively dropped)

The ACL blocks **all transit traffic entering from eth2** (the backbone-facing link), except one specific HTTP permit for `172.16.10.0/24 → 172.18.51.1:80`. Return traffic for pc15→pc11 (reply ICMP entering eth2) and all forward traffic from the backbone toward 172.18.51.0/24 enter eth2 and hit the DROP rules.

This matches the `acl-skill` fault family. Phase 5:

